lifeos-nix patch f-pulse-preflight-tilde — cron preflight resolves ~ paths

PROBLEM
  pulse.ts's cron preflight (issue #1392) disables any job whose referenced script
  file does not exist on this install. It resolves each script ref with
  `p.startsWith("/") ? p : join(PULSE_DIR, p)` — a path is treated as either absolute
  (leading "/") or relative to PULSE_DIR. A ~-prefixed path is NEITHER: "~/.claude/…"
  does not start with "/", so it is joined onto PULSE_DIR, yielding the nonsense path
  "<PULSE_DIR>/~/.claude/…", which never exists. The job is then falsely flagged
  missing and disabled at every boot — even though the script IS present and the shell
  would expand ~ fine at execution time. Only the preflight gate is broken; execution
  is not.

  Impact on the migrated box (2026-08-26): five user-tier jobs referencing ~/.claude/…
  paths — deriver, synthesis, conduit-capture, conduit-insight, derived-sync-fallback —
  were silently disabled at every startup since 2026-08-09. The whole autonomic layer
  (learning-hypothesis generation, weekly synthesis, derived-sync safety-net) was dead,
  with only a warn log to show for it. The base PULSE.toml uses only PULSE_DIR-relative
  commands, so vanilla never trips it, but any ~-path in a user job does.

FIX (1 file)
  pulse.ts — expand a leading "~/" to the home directory before the existence check.
  A new `resolveRef` helper maps "~/x" → join(homedir(), "x") and keeps the existing
  "/" (absolute) and PULSE_DIR-relative branches unchanged. Adds
  `import { homedir } from "os"`. The execution path is untouched (the shell already
  expands ~). Fixes the preflight false-negative for every install, not just ours.

VERIFICATION
  Unit: a job whose command references a ~/… script that EXISTS survives preflight
  (not added to missingScriptJobs); a genuinely-absent ~/… script is still flagged.
  Build: nix build green; egress-test + smoke unchanged. Live: after deploy + sync,
  /healthz no longer lists deriver / synthesis / derived-sync-fallback as disabled.

diff --git a/LifeOS/install/LIFEOS/PULSE/pulse.ts b/LifeOS/install/LIFEOS/PULSE/pulse.ts
--- a/LifeOS/install/LIFEOS/PULSE/pulse.ts
+++ b/LifeOS/install/LIFEOS/PULSE/pulse.ts
@@ -16,6 +16,7 @@
 
 import { join } from "path"
 import { readFileSync, existsSync } from "fs"
+import { homedir } from "os"
 import { parse } from "smol-toml"
 import { loadLifeosConfig } from "../TOOLS/LifeosConfig"
 import { isLoopbackHostHeader } from "./lib/host-guard.ts"
@@ -878,7 +879,9 @@
   for (const job of config.jobs) {
     if (!job.enabled || job.type === "claude" || !job.command) continue
     const scriptRefs = job.command.match(/[^\s'"]+\.(?:ts|js|sh)\b/g) ?? []
-    const missing = scriptRefs.filter((p) => !existsSync(p.startsWith("/") ? p : join(PULSE_DIR, p)))
+    const resolveRef = (p: string) =>
+      p.startsWith("~/") ? join(homedir(), p.slice(2)) : p.startsWith("/") ? p : join(PULSE_DIR, p)
+    const missing = scriptRefs.filter((p) => !existsSync(resolveRef(p)))
     if (missing.length > 0) {
       missingScriptJobs.add(job.name)
       log("warn", `Disabling cron job ${job.name}: script not present on this install`, {
